CHECK | func_80010BD8 | 80010c58 | outer loop step addiu $s2, $s2, 0x10 is the distance between the two 4-pointer arrays 0x80069EF0 and 0x80069F00 (2 buffers x 4 models); once each holds 6 model pointers this step must equal the new distance (0x18 if the two arrays are placed back to back). func_80010A50 has the same 2x4 clear loop (inner uVar3 < 4, outer step 0x10) and also needs 6 / the new step; func_80010C84 indexes 0x80069EF0/0x80069F00 by model
CHECK | func_80025F40 | 80026474 | the same 4 attached objects (0x80088278/0x8008826F) and shadow objects (0x80088748/0x80088F11) are set up by uVar8 < 4 loops in func_80023E9C and func_80024AE4 (not in this list); they must go to 6 as well. The (model,node) byte pairs 0x8008826F/0x80088270 (stride 2) sit right in front of the 0x80088278 object array, so 6 entries do not fit at the old address
NOT_SLOT | func_8001E3A8 | uVar6 < 4 (sprites 0x8007AC40 stride 0xDC / 0x8007AFB0 stride 0x34) | fixed 4-piece animated 2D graphic: func_8001E488 builds the 4 parts from constant tables 0x800500E8/0x800500F0 with part 3 special-cased, func_8001DF38 animates part 0..3 differently; nothing indexed by slot, port or model
NOT_SLOT | func_8001E3A8 | uVar5 < 3 inside uVar6 < 2 (0x8007B080 / 0x8007B5A8) | 2 groups x 3 sprites built from constant tables 0x8005004C/0x80050058 in func_8001E488; same 2D layer as above, no slot data
NEEDS_REWRITE | func_80018258 | 800182ac | one loop clears both per-PORT rumble arrays (0x80076568 stride 4, 0x800A10CC; func_80018480(port) indexes both by controller port) and the per-SLOT byte array 0x8009ED20 (func_80017780(slot)). sltiu 0x4 -> 0x6 would zero 0x80076578..0x8007657F (another variable, used by func_8001692C) and 0x800A10D0/D1; slots 4/5 of 0x8009ED20 need a separate clear (or keep this loop at 4 and clear them elsewhere)
NEEDS_REWRITE | func_800DBA88 | 800dbaf0 | scans bits 0..3 of DAT_800A10EC for the last set bit and uses it as a model index; those bits come from winner table 0x8014637C = {1,2,4,8} in func_80118A20 and bits 4..7 are LOSER bits (0x80146384 = {0x10,0x20,0x40,0x80}), bits 8+ are flags (0x100/0x200/0x400, 0x2000/0x4000). Raising the bound to 6 would read slot 0/1 loser bits as winners even in a 4-man match. Needs a new mask layout (6 winner bits, 6 loser bits elsewhere) shared with func_80118A20, func_80119C28 and every other reader of 0x800A10EC; then this sltiu becomes 0x6
NEEDS_REWRITE | func_80116130 | 801161d4 | builds a u16 camera/framing mask: bit i (0x1<<i) = slot i in play, 0x10 and 0x20 = flags, 0x40<<i = slot i eliminated. Slots 4 and 5 would set 0x10/0x20 (collide with the flags) and 0x400/0x800. The count slti 0x4 -> 0x6 is harmless for 4-man (slots 4/5 empty, no bits) but the layout must be redesigned for 6 together with its readers (func_800E30D8 xori 0x3C0 / >>6 / &0xF, and func_800EE594 which returns the same kind of mask)
CHECK | func_800E30D8 | 800e315c, 800e3178, 800e3184, 800e318c | mask constants tied to func_80116130/func_800EE594 layout: xori 0x3C0 (eliminated bits 6..9) then srl 6, andi 0xF / ori 0xF (all 4 slots). With 6 slots these become a 6-bit field (0x3F) and the eliminated-bit field moves; the srl shift amount is an R-type sa field. The PATCH at 800e3298 is safe for 4-man as is (0x8016B920[4..5] < 0 skips slots 4/5)
NEEDS_REWRITE | func_800E0304 | 800e0730 (sltiu $v0, $s1, 0x2), 800e070c..800e0718 | team score loop: 2 teams, team t = func_80117F14(2t) + func_80117F14(2t+1) (slot pairs {0,1},{2,3}). For 3 tag teams of 2 only the count changes (sltiu 0x2 -> 0x3; the buffer has room); for 2 teams of 3 the pairing (sll $a0, $s1, 1 / $s2 += 2) must be rewritten
CHECK | func_800E0304 | 800e06e0, 800e0790 | local short buffer at sp+0x20 (stored via 0x10($s0), $s0 = sp+0x10) grows from 4 to 6 shorts (sp+0x20..0x2B); sp+0x28..0x2F is unused in this frame (saved $s0 at 0x30), so it fits. The consumer func_800E0A0C reads it with a count of 2/3/4 from the match type and must accept 6
CHECK | func_800DEAB0 | 800ddb70 (func_800DDB10) | both loops use uVar3 < DAT_80158E98 (no immediate here); the count is set in func_800DDB10 (param, = 4 via addiu $v0, $zero, 0x4 for 0x6000 modes, 3 for 0x28000, 2 for 0x11000, +1 for 0x80000) and must be 6 for 6-man there
CHECK | func_800DEAB0 | 800dec08, 800dec20, 800dec9c, 800decd8, 800ded38 | HUD panel position = entry byte (0x80154638 stride 0xC) & 3 into 4-entry corner tables 0x80144BD0/0x80144BD8 (x {0x30,0x30,0x14F,0x14F}, y {0x14,0xCB,0x14,0xCB}), 0x80144BE0/0x80144BE8, 0x80144B78: 6 panels need 6 positions (bigger tables and andi 0x7). The fixed 4-entry orders written at 800deaf4..800deb1c (tag, 1/3/2/0) and 800deb34..800deb5c (0x28000) cover only entries 0..3
CHECK | func_800EC484 | 800ec4bc | local candidate array sp+0x10 (stride 0xC) holds at most 5 entries (6 slots minus self) at sp+0x10..0x4B after the swap temp is moved to sp+0x4C..0x57; for 4-man the extra entry 4 stays -1 so results are unchanged
CHECK | func_800EDCF4 | 800edd90 | with $fp = sp+0x8 the distance array uses sp+0xC..0x1F; sp+0xC is in this frame's outgoing-argument area, which is safe only because the one call made while the array is live (func_8012EA74 -> func_8012ECA0/func_8012ED0C) never stores to its caller's arg area. Global slot list 0x80159608 grows to 6 ints (0x80159608..0x8015961F) and would overlap the costume shorts at 0x8015961C if not moved
CHECK | func_80113E30 | 80113f58 | the count-down start address addiu $v0, $v0, -0x12EA (= 0x8009ED16 = base 0x8009ED10 + 3*2) must point to element 5 (new base + 0xA) when the address is rewritten
CHECK | func_80113E30 | 80114184, 8011418c, 80114194, 8011419c, 80114208 | tag-apron setup inside the second loop: slti $v0, $s0, 0x2 (slots >= 2 are partners on the apron, partner table (slot & 1)*0x40 at 0x8009FEA6/0x8009FEAB) and xori $v0, $s0, 0x3 (slot 3 special for 0x20000 mode). With the loop at 6 these also mark slots 4/5 (+0xE9/+0xF1 = 2) in tag modes; harmless for 4-man since the struct is empty, but a 6-man tag layout needs this logic revisited
CHECK | func_80113E30 | 80113ec4..80113ee8 | RNG seed = sum of the 4 roster ids 0x800A4038..0x800A4044 (unrolled); keeping 4 gives identical 4-man behaviour
NEEDS_REWRITE | func_80118A20 | 80118ab0, 80118cbc, 80118fd4 | not slot-count loops: they walk the caller's winner/loser lists (max 3 entries, ended by -1). Callers pass 4-int stack arrays (func_80117438 aiStack_f8/e8) or 2-3-int ones (func_80116CDC sp+0x10/0x18, func_80116328), and the first loop advances unconditionally, so raising 3 to 5 would read past the caller buffers (e.g. saved $s0 at sp+0x28 in func_80116CDC). Keep 3 if no side can have more than 3 wrestlers (e.g. 3v3); a side of 4-5 needs bigger caller buffers first
NEEDS_REWRITE | func_80118A20 | 80118bcc..80118c18 | unrolled 4x clear of +0x94 bit 2 (0x80159A24, 0x80159D7C, 0x8015A0D4, 0x8015A42C = slots 0..3); slots 4/5 are not cleared and there are no spare instructions
CHECK | func_80118A20 | 801191d0 | DAT_8009FE68 |= 0x80146580[slot] (table {4,8,0x10,0x20}) needs 6 entries; the next bits 0x40/0x80 are not free (func_800EE1E4 sets 0x40 in 0x8009FE68). Bits 1/2 are hard-wired to slot 0/1 at 80119090..801190dc. Mask tables 0x8014637C/0x80146384 (winner/loser bits) are covered under func_800DBA88
CHECK | func_8011D400 | 8011d464, 8011d470, 8011d4ac | hard-coded tag slot pairs passed to func_8011D5D0 (3,1), (2,0), (3,2) for 0x1000/0x20000 modes; fine for 4-man, need review for 6-man tag layouts
